# Benchmark: track what defines a run and what it concluded, never the payloads.
#
# Written as ignore-everything-then-re-include because git does not descend into
# an excluded directory: each level must be opened with `dir/*` before any child
# of it can be un-ignored. Keep that shape when adding a benchmark.
#
# biomysterybench/upstream/, spatialbench/ and compbiobench-runner/ are separate
# clones carrying their own .git — they stay out entirely. They are not
# submodules, and 4.6G of LFS-backed data zips does not belong in this history.
#
# `benchmark/*` matches direct children only, so upstream/ — one level deeper
# since the 2026-07-25 consolidation — needs its own `biomysterybench/*` line to
# stay excluded. Without it the whole HF clone becomes trackable.
benchmark/*
!benchmark/*.py
!benchmark/biomysterybench/
benchmark/biomysterybench/*
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/

# Spatial CellBench is tracked in full — `benchmark/*` above would otherwise
# hide the whole tree — minus its runtime artifacts.
!benchmark/spatial_cellbench/
benchmark/spatial_cellbench/runs/
benchmark/spatial_cellbench/slurm/*.out

# Optimizer CCC benchmark: track the harness, manifests, and the committed
# expert references (the accuracy oracle); never run payloads or work dirs.
!benchmark/optimizer_ccc/
benchmark/optimizer_ccc/runs/
benchmark/optimizer_ccc/reference/*/work/
benchmark/optimizer_ccc/reference/*.log
benchmark/optimizer_ccc/reference/*/*.log

# The problem set, the harness, and the graded results. `slurm/make_prompt.py`
# matters more than its size suggests: the preamble it emits is what separates
# one prompt version from another, and results are only comparable within a version.
benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/*
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/*.md
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/*.csv
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/grade.py
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/slurm/
benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/slurm/logs/

# Per-run archives: metrics.json, grade.json and the agent's own write-up —
# ~190K for the whole sweep. The terminal trace, chat dump, tables, figures and
# notebook run to megabytes per run and stay local; mine them in place. Note
# that metrics.json carries the verbatim prompt, so the prompt version a run uses is
# recoverable from the committed data alone.
#
# Both archive layouts are covered, and depth-agnostically, because they differ:
# run_problem.sh writes tissueagent_runs/<id>/ while run_one.sh:34 writes
# runs/<model>/<id>/<seed>/. `grade.py` rglobs for metrics.json and accepts
# either, so a depth-specific rule here would silently drop a whole model×seed
# sweep out of the history. `**/` re-opens every directory below the archive
# root — git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded — and
# only then are the three keepers un-ignored.
# The trailing `*` on tissueagent_runs matches retired sweeps too — they are
# renamed in place to tissueagent_runs_<date>_<version>/ rather than deleted
# (e.g. tissueagent_runs_2026-07-25_v0/). A retired version's metrics must stay
# in history or the version comparison in results.md becomes unverifiable.
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/tissueagent_runs*/
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/runs/
benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/tissueagent_runs*/**
benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/runs/**
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/tissueagent_runs*/**/
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/runs/**/
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/**/metrics.json
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/**/grade.json
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/**/attempts.jsonl
!benchmark/biomysterybench/biomysterybench_expr/**/reports/**/*.md

workspace/cellvoyager_agent/

